#Project description

This project analyzes customer churn for StreamWorks Media, a UK based video streaming platform. The goal is to identify who is churning, 
why they are leaving, and how the business can intervene early to reduce cancellations.

Using subscriber level data, the project performs data cleaning, feature engineering, and exploratory analysis to uncover churn patterns 
related to usage behavior, tenure, pricing, complaints, and engagement channels. Statistical tests are applied to validate key relationships,
such as the impact of watch time, promotions, and referrals on churn.

The project builds a logistic regression model to predict churn probability and a linear regression model to analyze factors affecting user 
watch time or tenure. Model performance is evaluated using standard classification and regression metrics. Findings are translated into clear
business insights and practical retention recommendations for decision makers.
